__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
# large regenerable data + build artifacts
*.parquet
data/*.db
data/*.db-journal
*.db-journal

# secrets (webhooks, API keys) live here — NEVER tracked
config.local.json
data/*.joblib

# weekly-runner local byproducts (launchd writes these on the Mac)
.venv/
data/logs/
data/manifests/

# data/snapshots/ IS TRACKED, deliberately. It is the immutable pre-kickoff
# record: what was published for each game before it started, the sha256 that
# proves the row has not moved since, and the freeze provenance. A record that
# exists only on one Mac cannot be audited by anyone — including by a future
# run of this repository — and the whole point of freezing at kickoff is that
# the pre-kickoff number is provable afterwards. An earlier revision ignored
# this directory; that decision is reversed here and in ops/LOAD_ME.md.
#
# Nothing in a snapshot carries a credential: predictions.csv is contract rows,
# snapshot.json holds a digest (a hash, never the source config it hashes),
# frozen.json holds published rows. The CFBD key lives in config.local.json,
# which stays ignored above.
#
# Only the rendered explainer is excluded: it is a presentation of
# predictions.csv, regenerable from it, and it is the bulk of the bytes.
data/snapshots/**/explainer.html

# team-season evidence build output — rebuild with
# scripts/build_team_evidence.py; the registry it is built from
# (data/team_evidence_registry.json) IS tracked.
data/team_evidence/
